# The operation takes its paths from the environment: no code decides them, so the files are known only by the
# environment variable that holds each (a hole the term names, never a guess). Three places all the same, by their variables;
# `read_pair` reads two and gives a str back to `join`, which writes the third.

route storage.run
step run/join
step run/join/Path                                          # `first = Path(os.environ["FIRST"])`
step run/join/Path#2
step run/join/Path#3
step run/join/read_pair

line entry > run call
line Disk({$FIRST}) > run/join/read_pair own
line Disk({$SECOND}) > run/join/read_pair own
line run/join/read_pair > run/join back
line run/join/Path > _·first@run/join/Path value
line run/join/Path#2 > _·second@run/join/Path#2 value
line run/join/Path#3 > _·destination@run/join/Path#3 value
line _·first@run/join/Path > run/join/read_pair value
line _·second@run/join/Path#2 > run/join/read_pair value
known #101 line _·destination@run/join/Path#3 > run/join value   # `destination.write_text(..)`
home _·first@run/join/Path run/join
home _·second@run/join/Path#2 run/join
home _·destination@run/join/Path#3 run/join
line run/join > Disk({$DESTINATION}) own

side entry left
side Disk({$FIRST}) left
side Disk({$SECOND}) left
side Disk({$DESTINATION}) right
